# Normalize line endings in the repository, and check out LF everywhere. Set for
# everything, so a file type added later needs no entry here.
#
# **`eol=lf` rather than "what the platform uses", and the difference is a
# failing gate.** Without it Windows checks out CRLF through `core.autocrlf`,
# and `.prettierrc.json` pins `endOfLine` to `lf` -- so `prettier --check`
# failed on **69 files at once** on the first Windows run of the format gate,
# before a single test had been reached. Nothing was wrong with any of them.
#
# The binary rules below re-clear `text` for their own patterns; the last
# matching line wins per attribute, so those keep `-text` and are never
# rewritten.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled addons and images carry bytes that a line-ending rewrite corrupts.
*.node binary
*.png  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
